{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for exact sales-design draft7 27f236d6eb0d88fe274cdedef5cae9bb1d96f85d / tree7c09906616bb5bdd88d67a0f4ab4f5b61eff3ada, sole primary32629660, notes/2026-10-19-sales-applications-design.md. Complete654-line primary read first in full. F1, F2 and F4 are resolved; two remaining corrections are F3 and F5.\n\nResolved F2: separate uniquely guarded open-price-approval/open-terms-approval acts now each open one item after the covered requirement exists. The single required import must be confirmed, mappings resolved, all rows reviewed/declined with reasons, both current approval items present, and rendering/assembly bound to that set. C3 includes missing/stale approvals and unresolved rows. This fits the existing opening/guard forms. Retain F1's fixed grants/assigned signer guards and F4's notice/index writes rather than deletion.\n\nF3 high — A publish-file request result is admission, not the later Git push result (5.2 lines370–394,5.3,5.4,6.2/6.3 and C3). The new result-clause path assumes a protocol today's runtime does not have. contract/src/entry.ts:99–100 defines Result as of{from,n}, outcome applied/refused/superseded and optional reason; it has no late push outcome or receipt binding payload. derive/src/delivery.ts:168–170 constructs that one result in the entry that decides the incoming request. The result verifier at296ff requires its authenticated source to be the delivery/genesis entry that decided that exact request; it does not accept a later operation outcome as a replacement result, and an already recorded result is terminal/repeated. Destination's publish-file handler opens a queued file-publication and judge work, whose push and public receipt happen later (platform/src/destination.ts:2581ff,2640ff,2672ff). The existing unknown/restart publication test demonstrates that outside push can remain unresolved. The lending example's publish declaration has result:{}, with no confirmation effects (examples/lending/definition.ts:490).\n\nConsequently an applied clause may safely record that Destination admitted this publication request, but cannot mark the file published, carry the claimed new tuple, or later turn a queued request into confirmed Git publication. Authenticating Destination as sender does not change what that deciding entry proves. Please remove the claim that today's result clause supplies late confirmed publication. For this first version, one supported small boundary is keeping native request/admission separate from the member's explicitly attributed check/report of the public Git receipt, without letting that report become independently destination-confirmed native state. Alternatively explicitly defer a shared confirmed-state transition until a real authenticated completion/readback protocol is designed and implemented; do not call that missing path today's existing publication behavior. Preserve pending/unknown, no blind resend, exact cause/path/digest matching in any actual receipt check, and member-report attribution. This requests an honest boundary, not commissioning a new integration framework.\n\nF5 medium — The new count policy works, but the byte policy still admits data that the complete read and file publication cannot carry (5.2 lines300–305 and5.4). One import,100 requirements, second-import refusal and replacement via a new bid room close the aggregate-row gap. However100 answers of4000 ASCII characters are400000 bytes by themselves, exceeding the262144-byte native ItemQuery/projection payload limit before the allowed128KiB input texts, drafts, identifiers, parties/refs and wire metadata. Later answer/draft growth is not bounded by an import-time cap on original texts. Characters also are not UTF-8 bytes. The sealed assembled text may independently exceed publish-file's65536-byte content limit.\n\nChoose conservative byte maxima over the full queried item representation throughout its lifecycle and over the final sealed text (or reduce the first-version row/text bounds), accounting for drafts/answers and serialization overhead. Reject an oversized later draft/answer/rendering before it strands the queue; do not imply that100rows alone or128KiB original input guarantees complete readable state. Narrowing the projected aliases does not remove the native ItemQuery payload limit that precedes projection. No increase to limits or generic paging is required. Existing constants are contract/src/item-query.ts:7, bytes/src/application-projection-types.ts:9–11, bytes/src/item-query-read.ts payload checks, and platform/src/destination.ts publish-file content max65536. The retained scratch arithmetic is a lower-bound counterexample, not a claim to have run a runtime suite.\n\nArchitecture conclusion: the proposed packages, split expert/team decisions, one bounded bid/import, ordinary approval openings, existing view kinds and multi-scope ownership are coherent and can fit current forms. The completion protocol claimed in F3 cannot. The reframed coordination section explains the product intent; its larger-matrix examples describe a broader motivation, not evidence that this bounded first version supports200rows. Nothing in the note's proposed package/hosted/archive scenarios is runtime acceptance.\n\nSecurity conclusion: fixed grants and assigned-party guards correctly separate agent drafting, expert supply, team review and management sealing. A genuine admission result and a genuine later Git receipt prove different acts; one must not be substituted for the other. Whole-room buyer exclusion and explicit source-file custody limits remain honest.\n\nSimplification conclusion: keep the resolved static actions, single import and ordinary openings. A smaller byte-safe first version and explicitly attributed external publication check are sufficient to avoid extending the runtime in this design. Defer any native completion protocol and larger responses as named dependencies rather than hiding them behind a result clause. Plan033 precedence remains unchanged and this review commissions no implementation.\n\nValidation: full final primary and changed sections inspected against prior drafts, sole Markdown path against Main2127, all10 local links/fragments resolve and whitespace clean. Primary SHA256a8c71b803e780c16302370a6ccb35a4881f4081bd18124c573fc9027ab42f899. Native prepare binds7f569087/28988cd9/report32629660 at this exact head. Scratch /private/tmp/checker-sales-design-jne3y8sq contains primary, diff, validation and byte counterexample. Actual landed Result construction/verification, Destination handler/outcome code and lending declaration read; no tests/gate rerun, source/test edits, package install, provider/publication/deployment action.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3262966030bbba05a6413e5afd00e993a8e216bf","binding":"assigned","head":"27f236d6eb0d88fe274cdedef5cae9bb1d96f85d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:82f4bdf16830c1e365dfc6b477175a2984aa2cb9\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:28988cd98dfb9eddaadb8934b253cc352c17814f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:82f4bdf16830c1e365dfc6b477175a2984aa2cb9","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}